dvisor_binary_local_dir | not`, which is not a valid boolean. So, I should change it to `when: not cadvisor_binary_local_dir` or `when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir | bool` but ensure it\'s a boolean.\n\nWait, perhaps the correct way is to use `when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir | bool` for Task 3 and `when: not cadvisor_binary_local_dir | bool` for Task 2. Alternatively, just `when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir` for Task 3 and `when: not cadvisor_binary_local_dir` for Task 2.\n\nI think the correct approach is to use `when: not cadvisor_binary_local_dir` for Task 2 to download only if the local directory is empty. For Task 3, `when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir` to copy if the directory exists.\n\nSo, I\'ll adjust the \'when\' conditions accordingly, replacing the problematic expressions with valid boolean checks. That should fix the yamllint errors without altering the intended functionality.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: create directories\n  file:\n    path: /opt/cadvisor\n    state: directory\n    mode: 0755\n\n- name: download cadvisor\n  url:\n    url: "{{ cadvisor_download }}"\n    dest: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor-{{ cadvisor_version }}\n    mode: 0755\n    validate_certs: yes\n    checksum: "{{ cadvisor_checksum }}"\n  when: not cadvisor_binary_local_dir\n\n- name: propagate locally distributed cadvisor binary\n  copy:\n    src: "{{ cadvisor_binary_local_dir }}/cadvisor-{{ cadvisor_version }}"\n    dest: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor-{{ cadvisor_version }}\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0755\n  when: cadvisor_binary_local_dir\n  notify: restart cadvisor\n\n- name: symlink cadvisor\n  file:\n    path: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor\n    state: link\n    target: /opt/cadvisor/cadvisor-{{ cadvisor_version }}\n    force: yes\n\n- name: server systemd service\n  template:\n    src: systemd-system-cadvisor-service.j2\n    dest: /etc/systemd/system/cadvisor.service\n    mode: 0644\n  notify: restart cadvisor\n\n- name: test_task\n  shell: systemctl status cadvisor.service\n  register: