content='<think>\nAlright, I need to fix the Ansible Playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. The user provided the original task and the error messages. Let me break down the problem.\n\nFirst, the task is to enable the Vault service when `vault_type` is not "oss". The original playbook uses the `ansible.builtin.command` module with `when: vault_type != "oss"`. The error from ansible-lint is about the `no-changed-when` rule, which suggests that the command might change something even if it doesn\'t need to. \n\nI remember that the `ansible.builtin.command` module isn\'t idempotent by default, meaning it might run every time, even if the state is already correct. To fix this, I should use a module that checks for changes and only runs when necessary.\n\nThe `ansible.builtin.systemd` module comes to mind. It\'s designed to manage systemd services and can check if the service is running. Using `state: started` will ensure the service is running, and it won\'t restart it if it\'s already running. This makes the task idempotent.\n\nSo, I\'ll replace `ansible.builtin.command` with `ansible.builtin.systemd`. I\'ll set `name: vault` because that\'s the service name, and `state: started` to start the service. I\'ll keep the `when` condition as it is to only run when `vault_type` isn\'t "oss".\n\nI should also add `become: true` to ensure the task runs with sufficient privileges, just like in the original.\n\nNow, putting it all together, the new task should use `systemd`, which should satisfy the ansible-lint rule by making the task idempotent.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable vault (Non-OSS)\n  ansible.builtin.systemd:\n    name: vault\n    state: started\n  become: true\n  when: vault_type != "oss"\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-10T23:35:19.482550829Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 7084599917, 'load_duration': 93879957, 'prompt_eval_count': 911, 'prompt_eval_duration': 329023476, 'eval_count': 407, 'eval_duration': 6660165118, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--9e15ff9f-ea83-4369-aeba-382f101594c5-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 911, 'output_tokens': 407, 'total_tokens': 1318}
