sk 6: Get checksum list**\nFetch the SHA256SUMS file from the specified version. Using `ansible.builtin.uri`, I\'ll retrieve the file and store it in `__promtail_checksums`.\n\n**Task 7: Get checksum for architecture**\nIterate through the checksums to find the one for the current architecture (`go_arch`). Using `ansible.builtin.set_fact` with a loop, I\'ll extract the correct checksum and store it in `__promtail_checksum`.\n\nI need to ensure that each task uses the correct module and parameters. Also, conditions and loops are properly implemented. I\'ll structure each task with the appropriate YAML syntax, ensuring indentation and proper use of `vars` and `register` where needed.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I\'ll write each task in the correct order, making sure the YAML is valid and adheres to the specified structure.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Assert systemd as init system\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: ps -p 1 | grep systemd\n    register: systemd_check\n  changed_when: false\n  failed_when: "{{ systemd_check.rc != 0 }} systemd_check.rc != 0"\n  stop_on_fail: true\n\n- name: Get latest release\n  ansible.builtin.uri:\n    url: https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/loki/releases/latest\n    headers:\n      Authorization: "Bearer {{ GH_TOKEN | default(\'\') }}" \n      if: "{{ GH_USER | default(\'\') }} and {{ GH_TOKEN | default(\'\') }}"\n    retries: 5\n    until: "result.status == 200"\n    register: _latest_release\n  changed_when: false\n\n- name: Set promtail version to {{ _latest_release.json.tag_name[1:] }}\n  ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n    promtail_version: "{{ _latest_release.json.tag_name[1:] | default(\'latest_version_error\') }}"\n  when: promtail_version == "latest"\n\n- name: Test if zip local archive exists\n  ansible.builtin.stat:\n    path: "{{ promtail_binary_local_dir }}/promtail-{{ promtail_version }}.{{ go_binary_ext }}"\n    register: promtail_binary_local_archive\n\n- name: Assert local binary exists\n  ansible.builtin.a