k 3: The module is 'file', again changing to 'ansible.builtin.file'. The state is 'absent', which is correct because we want to remove the file.\n\nI think that's all. Now, I'll rewrite the playbook with these changes, keeping the task order and other parameters the same.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  ansible.builtin.import_tasks:\n    file: files/assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  register: assertions_result\n\n- name: Disable automatic service management\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d\n    state: file\n    content: exit 101\n    mode: '755'\n  when: apt_autostart_state == 'disabled'\n\n- name: Enable automatic service management\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d\n    state: absent\n  when: apt_autostart_state == 'enabled'\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T01:36:53.604698092Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12673115922, 'load_duration': 90445137, 'prompt_eval_count': 1746, 'prompt_eval_duration': 908556444, 'eval_count': 682, 'eval_duration': 11672231438, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--c8f7af1b-240a-4cb7-8333-f1a592aaec93-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1746, 'output_tokens': 682, 'total_tokens': 2428}
