's necessary. The variables rke2_download_kubeconf_path, rke2_download_kubeconf_file_name, and rke2_api_ip will be used as specified.\n\nLet me outline the structure:\n\n1. The playbook starts with \'---\'\n2. Task 1: fetch module with the given parameters and conditions.\n3. Task 2: replace module with the specified regex and replacement, delegated to localhost, with the same conditions.\n\nI think that covers all the requirements. Now, I\'ll format this into the YAML playbook, ensuring each task is correctly structured and that all conditions and variables are properly set.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Download RKE2 kubeconfig to localhost\n  fetch:\n    src: /etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml\n    dest: "{{ rke2_download_kubeconf_path }}/{{ rke2_download_kubeconf_file_name }}"\n    flat: yes\n  when:\n    - rke2_download_kubeconf\n    - inventory_hostname == groups[\'rke2_servers_group_name\'][0]\n\n- name: Replace loopback IP by master server IP\n  replace:\n    path: "{{ rke2_download_kubeconf_path }}/{{ rke2_download_kubeconf_file_name }}"\n    regexp: \'(127\\.0\\.0\\.1|::1)\'\n    replace: "{{ rke2_api_ip | default(ansible_host) }}"\n    dest: "{{ rke2_download_kubeconf_path }}/{{ rke2_download_kubeconf_file_name }}"\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  become: false\n  ansible_check_mode: skip\n  when:\n    - rke2_download_kubeconf\n    - inventory_hostname == groups[\'rke2_servers_group_name\'][0]\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T01:58:31.697033801Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14810495331, 'load_duration': 86677483, 'prompt_eval_count': 607, 'prompt_eval_duration': 267459972, 'eval_count': 811, 'eval_duration': 14454919297, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--851a6776-c361-4691-9129-496ce60ed642-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 607, 'output_tokens': 811, 'total_tokens': 1418}
