content='<think>\nAlright, I need to figure out how to create an Ansible Playbook based on the user\'s instructions. Let\'s break down the requirements.\n\nFirst, the playbook must start with \'---\' on the first line. That\'s straightforward. It should be a valid YAML file, so I need to ensure proper syntax and structure.\n\nThe user mentioned that the playbook should be structured to be included in an Ansible Role, specifically under the tasks/ directory. That means I should organize the tasks correctly, without any playbook-level headers like hosts or vars. Only tasks should be present.\n\nThere are two tasks to include. \n\nTask 1 is to gather service facts. I remember that Ansible has a module called \'service_facts\' which is exactly for this purpose. So I\'ll use that module in the first task.\n\nTask 2 is a bit more complex. It needs to set the \'active_server\' variable. The description says it should iterate through the \'rke2_cluster_group_name\' group, delegate to each host, and set the fact only if the current host is in \'rke2_servers_group_name\' and the \'rke2-server.service\' is running.\n\nSo for Task 2, I\'ll use a loop with \'rke2_cluster_group_name\' as the variable. Inside the loop, I\'ll delegate the connection to each \'item\'. Then, I\'ll check if the current host is in \'rke2_servers_group_name\' and if the service is running. If both conditions are met, I\'ll set the \'active_server\' fact to the \'inventory_hostname\'.\n\nI need to ensure that the tasks are in the correct order and that the modules are used properly. Also, I must avoid adding any unnecessary comments or explanations, just the YAML tasks.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll start with \'---\', then list the tasks with their respective modules and arguments. I\'ll make sure the YAML is properly formatted, with each task as a dictionary under the \'tasks\' key.\n\nI should also check for any potential errors, like incorrect variable names or wrong module usage. For example, ensuring that \'rke2_cluster_group_name\' and \'rke2_servers_group_name\' are correctly referenced.\n\nFinally, I\'ll review the structure to confirm it\'s valid for an Ansible Role, ensuring it can be included without issues in the tasks/main.yml file.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Gather service facts\n  service_facts:\n\n- name: Set the active_server variable\n  loop: "{{ rke2_cluster_group_name }}"\n  delegate_to: "{{ item }}"\n  block:\n    - name: Check if current host is a server and service is running\n      set_fact:\n        active_server: "{{ inventory_hostname }}" \n      when:\n        - "{{ inventory_hostname }}" in "{{ rke2_servers_group_name }}"\n        - service(\'rke2-server.service\').state == \'running\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T02:12:31.557207771Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11042235952, 'load_duration': 2487474609, 'prompt_eval_count': 360, 'prompt_eval_duration': 277878365, 'eval_count': 597, 'eval_duration': 8275595269, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--cbc23e94-141b-441d-8277-fb9a44b98f65-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 360, 'output_tokens': 597, 'total_tokens': 957}
