content="<think>\nAlright, I need to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let me go through each task step by step to ensure I understand what's required.\n\nFirst, Task 1 is to create a system group named 'etcd'. I remember that in Ansible, the group module is used for managing groups. The state should be 'present' to ensure the group exists. So, the task will be straightforward: use group module with name etcd and state present.\n\nNext, Task 2 is about creating a user 'etcd', assigning it to the 'etcd' group, setting the shell to /bin/nologin, adding a comment, and ensuring the user exists. I'll use the user module here. The group is already created in the previous task, so I can reference it in the groups parameter. The shell and comment fields need to be specified, and state should be present.\n\nMoving on to Task 3, which involves copying a config file for kernel hardening. The file is named rke2-cis-sysctl.conf and needs to be placed in /etc/sysctl.d/60-rke2-cis.conf with mode 0600. The source path depends on whether /usr/local/share/rke2/ is writeable and the result of a partition check, which is stored in the variable partition_result.rc. I should use the copy module with remote_src set to yes. Also, after copying, I need to notify the handler 'Restart systemd-sysctl' to ensure the changes are applied.\n\nLastly, Task 4 is to flush all handlers. This is a standard Ansible task where the meta module is used with command set to flush_handlers. This ensures any pending handlers are executed immediately.\n\nI need to structure each task correctly, making sure the YAML syntax is valid. Since this is for an Ansible Role, the tasks should be in tasks/main.yml. I'll start each task with a dash and use proper indentation.\n\nI should also check for any variables or conditions. For Task 3, the source path might vary, but since the user is instructed to use remote_src, I'll set remote_src: yes. The notify parameter will trigger the handler after the file is copied.\n\nPutting it all together, I'll start the playbook with '---' and list each task in the specified order. I'll make sure there are no extra comments or explanations, just the YAML tasks as required.\n\nI think that covers all the tasks. Now, I'll write out the playbook accordingly, ensuring each task is correctly formatted and adheres to the instructions provided.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create etcd group\n  group:\n    name: etcd\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create etcd user\n  user:\n    name: etcd\n    group: etcd\n    shell: /bin/nologin\n    comment: 'Etcd system user'\n    state: present\n\n- name: Copy systemctl config file for kernel hardening\n  copy:\n    remote_src: yes\n    src: /usr/local/share/rke2/rke2-cis-sysctl.conf\n    dest: /etc/sysctl.d/60-rke2-cis.conf\n    mode: 0600\n  notify: Restart systemd-sysctl\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  meta:\n    flush_handlers: true\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T02:22:09.589152623Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12512496944, 'load_duration': 78231807, 'prompt_eval_count': 456, 'prompt_eval_duration': 117315605, 'eval_count': 702, 'eval_duration': 12315254643, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--3d2adfee-8f67-4f92-b002-8ea872985786-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 456, 'output_tokens': 702, 'total_tokens': 1158}
