 specified order, ensuring each has the exact names and modules as described. I\'ll avoid any additional tasks or modifications.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure the YAML is correctly formatted, with proper indentation and no linting issues. The playbook should be self-contained and ready to be included in an Ansible Role.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Copy kube-vip load balancer manifests to first server\n  copy:\n    remote_src: true\n    src: "{{kube_vip_cloud_provider}}/kube-vip-cloud-*.j2"\n    dest: "{{rke2_data_path}}/server/manifests/"\n    owner: root\n    mode: 0664\n  when: rke2_kubevip_cloud_provider_enable | default(false)\n\n- name: Ensure kube-vip manifest files have correct permissions\n  file:\n    path: "{{rke2_data_path}}/server/manifests/kube-vip-cloud-*.j2"\n    owner: root\n    mode: 0664\n    state: file\n  when: rke2_kubevip_cloud_provider_enable | default(false)\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-11T02:30:30.966792212Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 11653007372, 'load_duration': 84078493, 'prompt_eval_count': 287, 'prompt_eval_duration': 76657595, 'eval_count': 683, 'eval_duration': 11491121426, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--3d675102-136f-48b9-b984-7765cbcca88c-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 287, 'output_tokens': 683, 'total_tokens': 970}
