e: keepalived' when using apt, and 'ansible.builtin.dnf' when using dnf. Also, remove the 'when' clause and use 'ansible_pkg_mgr' to determine which package manager to use.\n\n4. Create directory: The 'file' module should be 'ansible.builtin.file' and the mode should be in decimal or quoted. So, mode: 0o755 or '755'.\n\n5. Template tasks: All template uses need to be changed to 'ansible.builtin.template'. Also, the 'dest' paths are correct, but I should ensure the modes are properly set, maybe as strings.\n\n6. Systemd task: Change to 'ansible.builtin.systemd' and ensure the parameters are correct. 'masked: false' is okay, but maybe it's better to set 'enabled: true'.\n\n7. Flush handlers: Use 'ansible.builtin.meta' with 'flush_handlers: true'.\n\nI also need to make sure that all module names are fully qualified and that any octal values are either converted to decimal or quoted. For example, mode: 0755 becomes mode: '0755' or mode: 755 (but in Ansible, it's usually treated as octal, so maybe 0o755 is better).\n\nLet me outline the changes step by step:\n\n- Replace all module names with their FQCNs.\n- Fix the package manager tasks to use conditionals based on ansible_pkg_mgr.\n- Change octal values to either 0o755 or quoted strings.\n- Remove the 'when' keyword and use 'ansible_pkg_mgr' variable.\n- Combine the apt and dnf install tasks into one with conditions.\n\nWait, in the original playbook, the 'Install packages' task was split into apt and yum, but the 'when' was used. I think it's better to have separate tasks but with the correct FQCNs and conditions.\n\nHmm, but ansible-lint is complaining about the 'when' parameter. Maybe I should remove it and rely on the 'ansible_pkg_mgr' variable.\n\nLet me try to structure each task correctly:\n\nFor the apt update, use 'ansible.builtin.apt' with 'update_cache: yes'.\n\nFor the dnf update, use 'ansible.builtin.dnf' with 'state: latest' and condition on ansible_pkg_mgr.\n\nFor installing packages, split into two tasks: one for apt and one for dnf, each with their conditions.\n\nBut the error was about 'when' being an invalid parameter for the apt module. So perhaps it's better to structure it without 'when' and use the package manager variable.\n\nWait, the 'ansible_pkg_mgr' variable is set by Ansible, so I can use that to conditionally run tasks.\n\nSo, for the install packages, I'll have two separate tasks: one for apt and one for dnf, each with their 'when' conditions.\n\nBut in the FQCN, I need to use 'ansible.builtin.apt' and 'ansible.builtin.dnf'.\n\nAlso, the original playbook had 'state: latest' in the apt_update and dnf tasks, which ansible-lint says should not use 'latest'. So I need to replace that with 'version' if possible, but for apt, it's 'update_cache: yes' to update the cache.\n\nI think I've covered all the issues. Now, I'll rewrite the playbook accordingly, ensuring all modules are FQCNs, conditions are correctly applied, and octal values are fixed.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Update apt cache\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    update_cache: yes\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'apt'\n\n- name: Update dnf cache\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    state: latest\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'dnf'\n\n- name: Install packages\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'apt'\n  register: keepalived_installation\n\n- name: Install packages\n  ansible.builtin.dnf:\n    name: keepalived\n    state: present\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == 'dnf'\n  register: keepalived_installation\n\n- name: Create directory for keepalived\n  ansible.builtin.file:\n    path: /etc/keepalived\n    state: directory\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0o755\n\n- name: Create Kubernetes API health check script for Debian OS family\n  ansible.builtin.template:\n    src: check_apiserver.sh.j2\n    dest: /etc/keepalived/check_apiserver.sh\n    owner: root\n    group: root\n    mode: 0o755\n  notify: Restart keepalived\n  when: ansible_os_family ==